{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790283511,"nonce":"CXDzXU7g90/LibEwPrirWsgMXkM=","title":"Python: map and filter as typed comprehensions wait on three comprehension defects","message":"The map/filter rewrite from p2-map-unknown-globals (map(f, xs) lowered as [f(x) for x in xs], typed by inference) was rejected four times because it routes calls through the comprehension path, which has pre-existing defects that the builtin path does not: (1) a comprehension over a set or frozenset iterates the set's raw storage (4e87aa2), so sorted(map(lambda v: -v, {3, 1, 2})) crashes; (2) the pending-exception check after the comprehension fires only when lowering marked a raise, and eval, sorted and round set the pending exception without marking it (a1692ee), so list(map(eval, ['1', 'q'])) prints before raising; (3) a typed list result does not widen when a value of another kind is appended (202606d, 222758d). Fix those three, then re-land the rewrite from refs/backup/wf_b2063457-04f-8/map-rewrite-full (commits 5ffcc5f5 sugar.rs part, 74d8f590, 7838a97c, bf1934ec: one binding analysis for shadowing, fixed callables only) and re-run the four rounds' edge programs (perf-designs-2026-09-21/p2_rounds.json lists them). It is what types scimark's N (fft about 2.2x faster on the NUC).","files":null}]}